ith coverage 0, there is a valid (x,y) cell with distance > r, hence t feasible.\n\nWe binary-search t in [0, (n-1) + (m-1)]. Each feasibility check runs a sweep with O(k) interval adds/removes and O((k + Umax) log Vsize) segment-tree updates, where Umax ≈ n + m, and Vsize ≈ n + m. This is efficient for the given constraints.\n\nThe final answer is the maximum t feasible.\n",
